---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Project membership and Production — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo">For Project admins</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Project membership and Production</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                Project admin includes Developer design rights and DevOps operate rights,
                plus project membership management for people <strong class="text-foreground">already on the team</strong>.
                You cannot create Identity logins, invite unknown emails, or create projects.
                Isolation is this project — catalogs from other projects 404.
            </p>

            <h2>Members</h2>
            <p>
                Exactly one role per (project, user): Developer, DevOps, or Admin. They
                are not nested. You place existing team users. Last explicit project admin
                may be removed only if at least one Team admin still covers the team.
                Removing someone writes audit snapshots (user id, email, display name)
                before membership rows disappear. History UI never requires the person to
                still be a member.
            </p>

            <h2>Production promote and approve</h2>
            <p>
                Production RequiresApproval. You see Production in the promote wizard.
                Approve and reject are ProjectAdmin on Web and API. DevOps cannot complete
                those actions even if a client posts the form. Rejection archives the
                target deployment.
            </p>

            <h2>What you still operate</h2>
            <p>
                Connections, deployments, schedules, agents, Git remotes, API keys, retry,
                and cone recovery. Interactive SQL may use any EnvironmentKind. Prefer
                not to treat Production preview as a substitute for a deployment run.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
